{"id": "EUVD-2026-102345", "enisaUuid": "41dc8522-35c8-38d1-a6e0-4dc98e6a5221", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE 2.7.1 through 2.9.0 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability in firewall_rules.php that allows remote attackers to inject script via the unencoded if parameter. When the non-default Require Firewall Interface option is enabled, attackers can lure users with firewall rules privileges into opening a crafted GET link to execute script in the WebGUI with their privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T20:02:04", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-rules-if-xss", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/firewall_rules.php#L138-L146", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/firewall_rules.php#L391", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-2.7.1-through-2.9.0-reflected-xss-via-firewall-rules-php"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hvrf-cf2c-3rqh", "CVE-2026-111233"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.06, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6405dc9c-3f1a-3f52-9a8a-e7ea79b1e5b2", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "2.7.1 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ca877d45-cbac-3274-b0ed-b2c16dbe3438", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}